<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of English Sunday league</p>
<p>(40 overs) cricket matches:</p>
<p>At Chesterfield: Derbyshire beat Glamorgan by eight wickets.</p>
<p>Glamorgan 103 in 27 overs (D.Cork 6-21). Derbyshire 106-2 in</p>
<p>19.1 overs.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Leicestershire beat Nottinghamshire by 87</p>
<p>runs. Leicestershire 252-9 innings closed (J.Whitaker 73).</p>
<p>Nottinghamshire 165 in 32.2 overs.</p>
<p>At Cheltenham: Gloucestershire beat Durham by five wickets.</p>
<p>Durham 226-7 innings closed (J.Lewis 102). Gloucestershire 230-5</p>
<p>in 37.4 overs (R.Russell 59 not out, T.Hancock 50).</p>
<p>At Lord's: Kent beat Middlesex by eight wickets. Middlesex</p>
<p>151-8 innings closed (K.Dutch 58). Kent 152-2 in 39.2 overs</p>
<p>(T.Ward 68 not out, A.Wells 56).</p>
<p>At Southampton: Lancashbire beat Hampshire by four wickets.</p>
<p>Hampshire 210-9 innings closed (M.Hayden 55). Lancashire 214-6</p>
<p>in 39.3 overs (N.Fairbrother 88).</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex v Worcestershire match tied.</p>
<p>Worcestershire 217 in 39.5 overs (T.Moody 59; S.Law 4-37). Essex</p>
<p>217 in 39.5 overs.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Northamptonshire beat Surrey by six wickets.</p>
<p>Surrey 206-7 innings closed (J.Ratcliffe 82; Mohammad Akram</p>
<p>4-19). Northamptonshire 208-5 in 38.3 overs (A.Penberthy 81).</p>
</text>
